From 6840ea658df3394f2b7e8feecc5c2ee950493f8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MasherDon <62326358+MasherDon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:02:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/92] moe-stream : skip the pairs outside a prefill wave by
 default

LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_WAVE_SKIP was opt-in since 94c17f8: exact, but on 2026-10-12 the drive was the limit of a
prefill in waves, so the compute it removes hid under the next wave's load. Since the expert files are no
longer mapped (3aa63fa, 74d0419) the drive delivers and the compute is the limit, and skipping wins at every
ubatch. DeepSeek V4.1-Flash Q2mix, prompts of 2159 / 8897 tokens, tok/s, skip vs park (SiegeLadder runs.md
4.23): -ub 2048 116 / 146 vs 57 / 60, -ub 1024 83 / 100 vs 57 / 62, -ub 512 55 / 64 vs 44 / 49.
KL against the -ub 512 io-1 reference on this build: mean 0, max 5.8e-5, same top-1 100%, PPL x1.000001.

LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_WAVE_SKIP=0 turns it off; any other value keeps it on, as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/llama-moe-stream.cpp | 13 ++++++++++---
 src/llama-moe-stream.h   |  2 +-
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/llama-moe-stream.cpp b/src/llama-moe-stream.cpp
index 5e24409..01511b8 100644
--- a/src/llama-moe-stream.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-moe-stream.cpp
@@ -506,10 +506,17 @@ llama_moe_stream::llama_moe_stream(uint32_t n_layer, uint32_t n_slots, int32_t n
     debug         = std::getenv("LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_DEBUG") != nullptr;
     use_direct_io = direct;
 
-    // opt-in: exact, but measured 2026-10-12 it does not speed up prompts (the disk is the limit) and at
-    // -ub 2048 the CUDA VMM pool then fails to grow (cuMemSetAccess: not ready) on an 8.9K prompt.
+    // On by default since 2026-10-14; LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_WAVE_SKIP=0 turns it off. Exact (KL at the noise
+    // floor, SiegeLadder runs.md 4.16). It was opt-in before: on 2026-10-12 the disk was the limit, so the
+    // wave compute it removes hid under the next wave's load, and at -ub 2048 the VMM pool failed to grow
+    // on an 8.9K prompt (fixed in fd3adec). Since the expert files stopped being mapped (3aa63fa, 74d0419)
+    // the compute is the limit: an 8.9K prompt with skipping vs without, measured 2026-10-14 (runs.md
+    // 4.23), -ub 2048 146 vs 60 tok/s, -ub 1024 100 vs 62, -ub 512 64 vs 49.
     // alloc_bufs() keeps it only when every expert cache lands in a CUDA buffer.
-    wave_skip = std::getenv("LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_WAVE_SKIP") != nullptr;
+    {
+        const char * s = std::getenv("LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_WAVE_SKIP");
+        wave_skip = s == nullptr || std::atoi(s) != 0;
+    }
 
     // Router bias toward resident experts. Read once here rather than per call so a run cannot
     // change policy halfway through and leave counters that describe two different experiments.
diff --git a/src/llama-moe-stream.h b/src/llama-moe-stream.h
index daa3ff0..e96582c 100644
--- a/src/llama-moe-stream.h
+++ b/src/llama-moe-stream.h
@@ -398,7 +398,7 @@ struct llama_moe_stream {
     int64_t n_shift_l2  = 0; // of those, substitutes found in the host tier
 
     // Multi-pass prefill skips the pairs outside the current wave rather than parking them (see
-    // llama_moe_stream_wave_skip). Opt-in with LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_WAVE_SKIP=1, and only where the
+    // llama_moe_stream_wave_skip). On unless LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_WAVE_SKIP=0, and only where the
     // expert caches live in a CUDA buffer, the one backend whose mul_mat_id handles skipped ids.
     // Exact either way - it changes which GEMM rows run, not what the model computes.
     bool wave_skip = false;
